    {
      "paths": [
        "private_file_identity_windows.rs"
      ],
      "finding": "Disk type, non-reparse tag, nonzero volume plus full 128-bit ID, object kind, not-delete-pending, positive timestamps/nonnegative lengths, and one-link regular files are checked. File snapshots compare full metadata plus security; directory comparison deliberately permits child-driven timestamps while retaining ID/security."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "private_file_security_windows.rs"
      ],
      "finding": "Effective thread token is preferred with process fallback only on ERROR_NO_TOKEN. Owner and bounded valid DACL are checked; unknown ACE kinds and foreign nonzero grants are rejected. No ACL repair is performed. Creation reuses the current protected-DACL helper without body change."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "private_artifacts_windows.rs"
      ],
      "finding": "New child creation is exclusive; locks deny writer/delete sharing and do not retry conflicting ownership. File writes/rename and directory barriers propagate errors, with post-operation checks. PrivateFile exposes neither raw handle nor writable File/Write capability; readonly construction cannot cast to writable directory."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "private_artifacts_windows_tests.rs"
      ],
      "finding": "Nine native cases retain hard assertions/expect failures, including identity/ACL/reparse/hardlink/name-alias/locking/atomic replacement boundaries. No ignore/skip-on-unsupported/soft-success substitution observed. Junction fixture correction invokes fixed cmd.exe arguments and validates actual reparse flag plus target before testing refusal."
    }
  ],
